; Stage 15 W9 defect 21: making protocols namespaced must not weaken the
; conformance CHECK. `Bad` has no `describe`, so `(extend Bad dp/Describe)` is
; still rejected — and the diagnostic names the protocol by its namespaced
; identity, which is what a reader needs when two namespaces declare a
; `Describe`. (Before defect 21 the same message said bare `Describe`, i.e. it
; could not tell you which protocol you failed to implement.)
(import-use "stdio.h")
(import-prefixed nsdescribe dpx)

(defstruct Bad n:i32)
(extend Bad dp/Describe)

(defn main ():i32 (return 0))
